-### Parameters and Typical Values
-- **Radius ($r$)**: Typically a positive float [G]. In examples, hardcoded values like $0.5$ or $1.0$ are common [S9, unofficial][S8, unofficial].
-- **Center ($c$)**: Typically $(0, 0, 0)$ for centered spheres [S1, unofficial][S9, unofficial]. Can be any 3D vector [G].
-- **Learnability**: In neural rendering contexts (e.g., NeRF variants), $c$ and $r$ may be treated as learnable parameters optimized during training [S4, unofficial][S5, unofficial][S6, unofficial].
